+++ b/features/todo-management.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,143 @@
+Feature: Todo Management
+  As a user
+  I want to create, complete, edit, and remove todos
+  So that I can track what I need to do
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is loaded
+
+  Rule: New todos
+
+  Scenario: Create a new todo
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    When the user types "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item with the title "Buy milk"
+    And the new-todo input is cleared
+
+  Scenario: Trim whitespace from new todo title
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    When the user types "   Buy milk   " into the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item with the title "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Ignore empty todo
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    When the user types "" into the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list remains empty
+
+  Rule: Completing todos
+
+  Scenario: Mark a todo as completed
+    Given the todo list has an item "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    Then the item "Buy milk" has the completed class
+    And its toggle checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Unmark a completed todo
+    Given the todo list has a completed item "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox for "Buy milk"
+    Then the item "Buy milk" does not have the completed class
+    And its toggle checkbox is not checked
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete
+
+  Scenario: Mark all todos as complete
+    Given the todo list has items "Buy milk", "Walk dog", "Write code"
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then every todo item has the completed class
+
+  Scenario: Unmark all todos via toggle-all
+    Given all todos are completed
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then no todo item has the completed class
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all reflects individual completions
+    Given the todo list has items "Buy milk", "Walk dog", "Write code"
+    When the user completes "Buy milk"
+    And the user completes "Walk dog"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+    When the user completes "Write code"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Rule: Deleting todos
+
+  Scenario: Delete a todo
+    Given the todo list has an item "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the destroy button for "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list does not contain "Buy milk"
+
+  Rule: Editing todos
+
+  Scenario: Enter edit mode on double-click
+    Given the todo list has an item "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy milk"
+    Then the item "Buy milk" has the editing class
+    And its edit input is focused
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on Enter
+    Given the todo list has an item "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy oat milk" into the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the item "Buy milk" does not appear in the todo list
+    And the todo list shows "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on blur
+    Given the todo list has an item "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy oat milk" into the edit input and presses Tab
+    Then the item "Buy milk" does not appear in the todo list
+    And the todo list shows "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Scenario: Cancel edit on Escape
+    Given the todo list has an item "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy oat milk" into the edit input and presses Escape
+    Then the todo list shows "Buy milk" unchanged
+    And the item "Buy milk" does not have the editing class
+
+  Scenario: Delete todo if edit is empty
+    Given the todo list has an item "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy milk"
+    And the user clears the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list does not contain "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Trim title on save
+    Given the todo list has an item "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "  Buy oat milk  " into the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Rule: Clear completed
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed todos
+    Given the todo list has items "Buy milk", "Walk dog", "Write code"
+    And "Buy milk" is completed
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+    When the user clicks the "Clear completed" button
+    Then the todo list contains "Write code"
+    And the todo list does not contain "Buy milk"
+    And the todo list does not contain "Walk dog"
+
+  Scenario: Hide clear-completed button when no completed todos
+    Given the todo list has an item "Buy milk" that is not completed
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Show clear-completed button when completed todos exist
+    Given the todo list has a completed item "Buy milk"
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is visible
+
+  Rule: Todo count
+
+  Scenario: Display active todo count
+    Given the todo list has items "Buy milk", "Walk dog", "Write code"
+    And "Buy milk" is completed
+    Then the todo-count shows "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Pluralize count correctly
+    Given the todo list has 1 active item "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo-count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Zero count when no active todos
+    Given the todo list has items "Buy milk", "Walk dog"
+    And "Buy milk" is completed
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+    Then the todo-count shows "0 items left"
