diff --git a/features/todo-persistence.feature b/features/todo-persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d29d229
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+Feature: Todo Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is loaded
+
+  Rule: localStorage persistence
+
+  Scenario: Save todos to localStorage
+    When the user types "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then localStorage has a key matching "todos-" with an entry for "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Restore todos from localStorage on reload
+    Given localStorage has a saved todo with title "Buy milk" that is not completed
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Persist todo completion state
+    Given the todo list has an item "Buy milk"
+    When the user completes "Buy milk"
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the item "Buy milk" has the completed class
+
+  Scenario: Persist todos across multiple sessions
+    Given the todo list has items "Buy milk", "Walk dog"
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    And "Walk dog" has the completed class
+
+  Scenario: Persist active filter on reload
+    Given the todo list has items "Buy milk", "Walk dog", "Write code"
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+    When the user clicks the "Active" filter link
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link has the selected class
+    And the todo list shows 2 items
+
+  Scenario: Remove deleted todos from localStorage
+    Given the todo list has items "Buy milk", "Walk dog"
+    When the user deletes "Buy milk"
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item "Walk dog"
+    And localStorage does not contain an entry for "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Do not persist editing state
+    Given the todo list has an item "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy milk"
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the item "Buy milk" does not have the editing class
+
+  Rule: localStorage format
+
+  Scenario: Use correct localStorage format
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    When the user types "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the localStorage entry for "todos-" contains an object with keys "id", "title", and "completed"
\ No newline at end of file
